cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Evidence Factory: Policy-as-Code for AI Act Compliance"
authors:
  - family-names: Brodwall
    given-names: Sarah
    affiliation: "Nav (Arbeids- og velferdsetaten / Norwegian Labour and Welfare Administration)"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-5575-3260"
repository-code: "https://github.com/navikt/evidence-factory"
url: "https://github.com/navikt/evidence-factory"
abstract: >-
  Evidence Factory is a proof-of-concept that treats AI Act governance
  requirements as executable policy. It encodes governance obligations as
  policy-as-code (OPA/Rego) and enforces them as CI/CD pipeline gates,
  turning compliance failures into build failures rather than narrative
  documentation. The project distinguishes verifiability (independent
  determination that compliance claims are true) from traceability
  (existence of linked artifacts), and frames the gap between them as
  an open research problem.
keywords:
  - AI Act  
  - AI governance
  - policy-as-code
  - compliance as infrastructure
  - evidence
  - OPA
  - Open Policy Agent
  - Rego
  - Conftest
  - verifiability
  - traceability
  - AI assurance
  - public sector AI
